 "sourceUrl": "https://e-file.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/0f9e00e3f2ca431693884a01667d7ec6/M3T1A669N1188254857740624027/OptiXtrans%20E9600%20Family%20-.pdf",
 "notes": "Slot count from two vendor documents: the E9600 family brochure (277,705 B) prints \"1:1 cross-connect mode: 12 large slots or 24 small slots\" / \"1:3 cross-connect mode: 10 large slots or 20 small slots\" with the note \"One 11 U slot of the E9624 subrack can be split into two 5.5 U slots\", and the TNG2DAP board chapter (871,676 B, 51 pp, V100R024C00) prints Table 1 \"Valid slots\" with the E9624 row \"1 | IU1 to IU24\" plus the footnote \"In the 1:3 mode of an E9624 subrack, service boards cannot be installed in slots IU6, IU7, IU18, and IU19\". The E9624 subrack chapter itself is not in the public document set (only E9605 and E9612 are), which is why the slot count is taken from the two documents above. Ports: TNG1N210 is \"10 x 10 Gbit/s Line Service Processing Board\" in the boards-overview Table 3 with E9624 \"1:1 mode: Y 1:3 mode: Y\"; 24 slots x 10 = 240, each a 10G optical line (OTU2/OTU2e) interface in an SFP+ cage. The cage is derived from the 10G optical line rate - the board datasheet with the front panel (EDOC1100163901) is behind the support wall. No fabric block is declared: the 1:1 cross-connect is 4.8 Tbit/s OSUflex/ODUk (brochure), above the 2.4 Tbit/s these 240 ports offer, so it caps nothing. Build provenance. The frame half is vendor-stated: `https://e-file.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/0f9e00e3f2ca431693884a01667d7ec6/M3T1A669N1188254857740624027/OptiXtrans%20E9600%20Family%20-.pdf` (Product Brochure, 277,705 B) prints the \"Max. number of service board slots\" row, and the subrack chapters print the slot map. The card half is vendor-stated too, but from a partner mirror rather than a Huawei host: `https://www.actfornet.com/solutions/solution/OptiXtrans_E9600_Boards_Overview` (HTTP 200, 226,637 B) reproduces the hedex chapter *OptiXtrans E9600 (E9624/E9612/E9605) Boards Overview* (`EDOC1100126589`) and carries Table 3, \"Mapping between the line boards and OptiXtrans 9800 E9624/E9612/E9605 subrack\", whose TNG1N206/TNG1N210 row reads E9624 \"1:1 mode: Y 1:3 mode: Y\", E9612 \"Y\", E9605 \"Y\". That is the board-to-subrack validity no Huawei-hosted document publishes (the board chapters answer 302 -> /view/notFound; see research/optixtrans-client-board-chapters.md). The complement is a build recorded here, not a vendor configuration: every service slot is filled with the same line board, the convention devices/huawei/optixtrans-e6616.json and devices/arista/7504r.json already use. A shelf with tributary (TNG1T212/TNG1A212) or WSS boards fitted in some slots is a different box with a different port list.",
 "aliases": [
  "E9624"
 ]
